{"parentUuid":"6cd426aa-4d96-4752-9cce-c71be0365983","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YTJgZ4ZrjdgZ6S5PJf6sQb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Swd6fjfseYuRy5nfiWQ1Fp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev/jar/overnight-exploration/MASTER-PORT-PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15745,"cache_read_input_tokens":8618,"output_tokens":159,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1880,"output_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":8618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbtLsdTmQtahyEnCQSfoM","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf5b8b63-6384-4946-b120-f8ceac1b778b","timestamp":"2026-06-09T20:48:31.885Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev","sessionId":"367791ef-ba0c-4f75-943f-87a55717b89c","version":"2.1.168","gitBranch":"lnstruct-migration-20260609"}
{"parentUuid":"cf5b8b63-6384-4946-b120-f8ceac1b778b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0ebc7be0-662c-445a-90fb-709dc278e9e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Swd6fjfseYuRy5nfiWQ1Fp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan / new-chat prompt — port the finalised SolverLNSimple optimisations onto `master`\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** plan only. Nothing here has been executed.\n4\t**Audience:** a fresh Claude Code chat that will implement it.\n5\t**Repo:** `/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev`. All paths relative to repo root.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 0. Objective\n10\t\n11\tLand the finalised SolverLNSimple performance optimisations on `master` as a\n12\tsmall sequence of clean, individually-verified commits — **grouped so each\n13\tcommit is one genuine change** — where each ported change is **byte-faithful to\n14\tthe validated implementation** and each step shows **no clear accuracy or\n15\tefficiency regression**.\n16\t\n17\tThree firm principles from the requester:\n18\t- **Only port code that is necessary and works.** No rejected accelerators, no\n19\t  sweep-knob plumbing, nothing not needed by the solver.\n20\t- **Fidelity over cleverness (for the logic).** The ported *logic* must match the\n21\t  code that was already validated. Do **not** re-derive it from scratch — extract\n22\t  the validated hunks (§4).\n23\t- **Fine-tune every number ourselves (for the constants).** The tunable values —\n24\t  convergence tolerance, the two under-relaxation α's, and the cycle-detector\n25\t  thresholds — are **re-derived by our own sweeps** on the verify branch (§6).\n26\t  The study's values are the *starting hypothesis*, not the answer to copy. Our\n27\t  first-party sweep is itself report data.\n28\t\n29\tPerformance is **not** strictly gated. We do not require the documented per-step\n30\tfigures to reproduce — different (grouped) order, re-tuned values. We require:\n31\tno clear regression, and a per-feature iteration-count + runtime-median delta\n32\trecorded wherever the signal is above noise.\n33\t\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t## 1. The finalised set, grouped into 8 commits\n37\t\n38\tThe finalised set is the 11 `overnight-perf-accumulate-2` KEPT changes + the one\n39\tsurviving struct slice (confirmed against `jar/perf-section-notes.md` §1–§4 and\n40\t`jar/overnight-exploration/CONSOLIDATED.md` §5). Below they are **grouped** —\n41\texploration changes that are genuinely one change are merged into a single\n42\tcommit. Subjects are deliberately **value-free**; the fine-tuned number each\n43\tcommit adopts goes in the commit body once our sweep (§6) selects it.\n44\t\n45\t| commit | subject (master style) | merges | report § | tunable value(s) | files |\n46\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n47\t| 1 | add limit-cycle detection to the outer fixed-point loop | **E2** | §1 | cycle `WINDOW`/`REL`/`DELTA_CAP` (conservative baseline) | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n48\t| 2 | cache LqnGraph topological queries | **E8 + S2-E1** | §2 | — | `LqnGraph.java` |\n49\t| 3 | cache per-network layer and class lookups, inline default sweep | **S2-E2 + S2-E3** | §2 | — | `MvaInputs.java`, `LqnGraph.java`, `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n50\t| 4 | read findCallerTask from the struct caller relation | struct slice (**replaces** part of #2 — see §4b) | §2 | — | `LqnGraph.java` |\n51\t| 5 | warm-start clients delays from a closed-form lqn estimate | **S2-E8** | §3 | — | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n52\t| 6 | drop fan-out caller and INF-task under-relaxation | **E7 + E12** | §4 | `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`, `D_RELAX_ALPHA` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n53\t| 7 | tighten the limit-cycle detection window | **E14** | §4 | cycle `WINDOW`, `REL` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n54\t| 8 | loosen convergence tolerance | **E10 + S2-E7** | §4 | `DEFAULT_TOL` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n55\t\n56\t(Study's hypothesis values, to test and likely confirm — **not** to copy\n57\tblindly: `DEFAULT_TOL=1.5e-2`, `Z_RELAX_ALPHA=D_RELAX_ALPHA=1.0`, cycle\n58\t`WINDOW=1`, `REL=1e-3`, `DELTA_CAP=10`.)\n59\t\n60\t**Why this order.**\n61\t- **Commit 1 leads — cycle detection is a genuine standalone first win.** At a\n62\t  conservative window it fixes the `A4_chainPlusFanout` maxIter pathology\n63\t  (100 → ~13 iters) on its own, is safe at master's α=0.5/tol=5e-3 (no α\n64\t  dependency), and matches the report's §1-first \"fix the algorithm before\n65\t  tuning\" framing. Its thresholds are set conservatively here and **fine-tuned in\n66\t  commit 7**.\n67\t- **Commits 2–4 are the §2 caches** (iteration-neutral). Commit 4 **replaces**\n68\t  part of commit 2 (the `findCallerTask` cache → struct read, §4b).\n69\t- **Commit 5 is warm-start** (§3); it must follow the caches (2–3) it consumes\n70\t  (perf-section-notes §3).\n71\t- **Commits 6–8 are the §4 convergence tuning.** The one hard constraint:\n72\t  **the under-relaxation value (commit 6) must precede the cycle-window tighten\n73\t  (commit 7) and the tolerance loosening (commit 8)** — those two are only safe\n74\t  once the per-iter step is un-damped (otherwise they false-fire / cross the\n75\t  accuracy cliff at the damped α). So the cycle-window tightening (E14) is\n76\t  deliberately deferred from commit 1 to commit 7: it is the *later tuning* of\n77\t  the detector, and it depends on the commit-6 α. Tolerance is swept and set\n78\t  **direct to its tuned value** (skipping the 1e-2 waypoint that only existed in\n79\t  the study's measurement journey).\n80\t\n81\tEndpoint (full chain, both corpora): 56 pass / 3 known-fails\n82\t(`B_scaleAxis_tasks5/10/20_fanout`, pre-existing on master), `regressions=0`,\n83\tconstants set to our **fine-tuned first-party values**. If those land on the\n84\tstudy's values the output is bit-identical to accumulate-2; if our sweep selects\n85\tdifferent values, the output stays within the LN accuracy envelope and our values\n86\tbecome the new reference (record the delta).\n87\t\n88\t---\n89\t\n90\t## 2. What to EXCLUDE (not necessary / does not belong)\n91\t\n92\t1. **Rejected accelerators** — all Anderson / Nesterov / Broyden / Aitken code\n93\t   and their fields/knobs. The report covers them as \"rejected alternatives\"; no\n94\t   production code.\n95\t2. **The 9 `System.getProperty` sweep knobs** (`lnsimple.tol`, `lnsimple.zalpha`,\n96\t   `lnsimple.dalpha`, `lnsimple.cycle*`, `lnsimple.warmStart`, `lnsimple.sweep`,\n97\t   `lnsimple.aitken`, …). On `master`, bake the fine-tuned values as constants —\n98\t   keep master's existing `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`/`D_RELAX_ALPHA`/`DEFAULT_TOL` names,\n99\t   just change the values; do **not** introduce the `readDoubleProp`/`*_DEFAULT`\n100\t   indirection. Knobs exist **only on the verify side-branch**, as the sweep\n101\t   harness (§6).\n102\t3. **`LayeredSolverResult.java` diagnostic-timing fields** (`lqnsElapsedTimeMs`\n103\t   etc.) — unrelated SolverLQNS fields that leaked into the accumulate-2 diff\n104\t   from skip-worktree local mods. Exclude.\n105\t4. **The FastEval harness + fixtures + CSVs from `master`** — verification tool,\n106\t   not a deliverable. Side-branch only (§3).\n107\t\n108\t---\n109\t\n110\t## 3. Branch strategy\n111\t\n112\tVerify (and sweep) on a side-branch; `master` receives only the production\n113\tcommits.\n114\t\n115\t```\n116\tmaster\n117\t  └── perf-port                ← do ALL work here\n118\t        V0 (test-only): FastEval + EvaluationSuite + util/DataCollector\n119\t                        + ln-reference.tables.csv + LQNS baseline CSV\n120\t        1..8: production commits (table above)\n121\t```\n122\t\n123\tWhen verified, replay 1–8 onto `master`\n124\t(`git rebase --onto master V0 perf-port`, or cherry-pick), dropping V0. `master`\n125\tends with 8 clean production commits.\n126\t\n127\tPull the harness + data from the exploration branches onto V0:\n128\t- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/overnight/FastEval.java`\n129\t- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/overnight/CaptureLnReference.java`\n130\t- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/util.java`\n131\t- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/DataCollector.java`\n132\t- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/fixtures/EvaluationSuite.java`\n133\t- `jar/overnight-exploration/data/ln-reference.tables.csv` (cached LN ref —\n134\t  copy it; ~287 s to regenerate otherwise)\n135\t- `report/data/f20axis-20260605T173243Z/baseline.tables.csv` (LQNS ref — copy\n136\t  if not already on `master`)\n137\t\n138\t(`git checkout overnight-perf-accumulate-2 -- <test path>`;\n139\t`git checkout overnight-perf-exploration -- <ln-reference csv>`.)\n140\t\n141\t**Setup risk to clear first:** FastEval reads SolverLNSimple's iteration count.\n142\tIf that accessor exists only in the modified solver, FastEval won't compile\n143\tagainst pristine `master`. Resolve in V0 (add the minimal read-only accessor, or\n144\tadapt FastEval), then confirm V0 builds + runs against **unmodified** master and\n145\tproduces a sane baseline before commit 1.\n146\t\n147\t---\n148\t\n149\t## 4. Fidelity method — port validated logic, then fine-tune the numbers\n150\t\n151\tSeparate the two concerns: the **logic** is ported faithfully; the **constants**\n152\tare our own.\n153\t\n154\t1. **Establish the faithful end-state first, using the study's values.** Take\n155\t   accumulate-2's `SolverLNSimple.java`, `LqnGraph.java`, `MvaInputs.java`;\n156\t   remove the accelerator/knob code (§2); set the tunable constants to the\n157\t   study's hypothesis values (`tol=1.5e-2`, `α=1.0`, `WINDOW=1`, `REL=1e-3`,\n158\t   `DELTA_CAP=10`); apply the struct `findCallerTask` change (§4b). Build + run\n159\t   FastEval. **With the study's values this must reproduce the validated result\n160\t   bit-identically** (56/3, regressions=0, iters 186/192). That proves the\n161\t   **logic** port is faithful — independent of what we later tune to. *Keep this\n162\t   as the logic-reference target.*\n163\t2. **Decompose into the 8 grouped commits**, starting from master, in the §1\n164\t   order. Each slice is lifted from the validated end-state code, so the kept\n165\t   logic is byte-faithful — you choose *when* each validated change appears, not\n166\t   rewrite it. For the commits that carry a tunable value (1, 6, 7, 8), run the\n167\t   sweep (§6) on the verify branch and **bake the value our sweep selects**, not\n168\t   the study's by default.\n169\t3. **End-state fidelity check (mandatory).** After commit 8,\n170\t   `git diff master..perf-port -- <the three solver files>` must equal the\n171\t   logic-reference diff from (1) **modulo the tunable constant values** — i.e.\n172\t   the kept logic, accelerator/knob removals, struct slice, and constants all\n173\t   present, with the constants holding *our* fine-tuned numbers. Anything else\n174\t   (logic that differs) is unintended divergence.\n175\t\n176\tJava 8 compatibility applies to all `jar/` production code (no `var`,\n177\t`Collectors.toList()` not `Stream.toList()`, etc. — CLAUDE.md).\n178\t\n179\t### 4a. Where each commit's diff lives (source map)\n180\t\n181\tRead with `git show <commit> -- <solver file>` (and, for a file's validated\n182\tend-state, `git diff master overnight-perf-accumulate-2 -- <file>`). Read, then\n183\tslice — do **not** cherry-pick out of order, context won't line up.\n184\t\n185\t| commit | merges | source commit(s) | branch | slicing notes |\n186\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n187\t| 1 | E2 | `e906ddaed` | accumulate-2 | cycle block + state vars; start at a conservative window/rel (study's `WINDOW=3, REL=1e-4, DELTA_CAP=10`) — fine-tuned in commit 7 |\n188\t| 2 | E8 | `ffbe2ed81` | accumulate-2 | name cache + `WeakHashMap` + volatile fast-path |\n189\t|   | S2-E1 | `8dee2893c` | accumulate-2 | the ~17 derived-quantity cache entries (same `ModelCache`) |\n190\t| 3 | S2-E2 | `27e58174b` | accumulate-2 | `LayerInfo` cache in MvaInputs + `invalidateAllLayerCaches` call in SolverLNSimple |\n191\t|   | S2-E3 | `7f888b418` | accumulate-2 | class-lookup caches + sibling-mean h