\t| `taskHasSyncCallees`, `callerFansOut`, `isInfScheduledTask`, `isInfProcessor`, `taskHasAndFork` | keep cached-OO — the full migration tried to delegate these and was **reverted/rejected**; only `findCallerTask` survived |\n213\t\n214\tCommit 4 adds: `callerOfT` (`int[]`, callee t-index → first sync-caller t-index),\n215\t`taskIndexByName` (`Map<String,Integer>`), `taskNameByT` (`String[]`), and\n216\t`buildCallerRelation(model, mc)` (derives all three from\n217\t`model.getStruct().issynccaller`, called from `cacheFor`). `findCallerTask`'s\n218\tbody becomes `name → taskIndexByName → callerOfT[t] → taskNameByT[caller]`.\n219\t\n220\t**Trap:** the `lqngraph-struct-migration` branch left `callerOfTask` *declared\n221\tbut dead* after the switch. Our clean port must delete it. After commit 4:\n222\t`grep callerOfTask` returns **nothing**; `grep callerOfT` returns the struct\n223\tarray. That grep is the no-overlap check.\n224\t\n225\tThe other caches (S2-E1 derived quantities in commit 2; S2-E2/E3 in commit 3)\n226\tare **not** touched by the struct slice — no overlap there.\n227\t\n228\t---\n229\t\n230\t## 5. Per-commit gate (relaxed — regressions only, plus recorded stats)\n231\t\n232\tAfter each commit, build (`cd jar && mvn -Dtmp=true compile -DskipTests`) and run\n233\tFastEval on the 59-fixture fast set. Gate:\n234\t\n235\t- **No accuracy regression** — 56 pass / 3 known-fails holds, `regressions=0`,\n236\t  per-fixture max-slack vs LN within tolerance. On the iteration-neutral commits\n237\t  (2, 3, 4) the output must be **bit-identical** to the previous commit; a slack\n238\t  change there means the port diverged — stop and fix. (Commit 5 warm-start may\n239\t  shift the trajectory but must stay within tolerance; commits 1, 6, 7, 8 change\n240\t  iters by design.)\n241\t- **No efficiency regression** — iteration count must not *increase* vs the\n242\t  previous commit, and runtime median must not *clearly* worsen (beyond the\n243\t  ~1.7× noise floor).\n244\t- **Do not require the documented chronological figures** — grouped/different\n245\t  order, re-tuned values; they won't match.\n246\t\n247\t**Per-feature stats (report deliverable, recorded not gated).** FastEval reports\n248\titers + runtime each run, so record per commit: iteration-count before→after,\n249\truntime median + [min,max] over ≥3 warmup + ≥5 timed runs, and — for commits 1,\n250\t6, 7, 8 — the **sweep curve** that selected the value (§6), which is first-party\n251\ttuning evidence for the report. Honest reading:\n252\t- Commit 1 (cycle detection): deterministic iter drop, headlined by\n253\t  `A4_chainPlusFanout` 100 → ~13 — the genuine standalone first win, citable.\n254\t- Commits 6, 7, 8: deterministic iter-count deltas at the chosen values — real,\n255\t  citable numbers, with our own sweep behind them.\n256\t- Commit 2: contains E8, the one clean wall-clock win vs master (large runtime\n257\t  drop). It also carries S2-E1's derived cache (load-bearing per\n258\t  perf-section-notes §2); per-layer attribution is via the ablation flags on the\n259\t  verify branch, not via the commit split.\n260\t- Commits 3, 4: within the 1.7× noise floor — log as \"within noise\", don't\n261\t  invent a win.\n262\t\n263\tA within-noise runtime wobble on a cache commit is expected and does **not** block\n264\tit; only a *clear* regression blocks.\n265\t\n266\t---\n267\t\n268\t## 6. Fine-tuning the values ourselves (required, on the verify branch)\n269\t\n270\tEvery tunable number is re-derived by our own sweep — the study's values are the\n271\thypothesis, not the answer. Mechanism: keep temporary `System.getProperty` knobs\n272\t**on the verify branch only**; sweep; then bake the selected value into the\n273\tproduction commit (which ships a bare constant, no knob).\n274\t\n275\tWhat to sweep, and how:\n276\t- **Commit 6 — under-relaxation `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`, `D_RELAX_ALPHA`.** Sweep each\n277\t  over (e.g.) {0.5, 0.7, 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.2}. Adopt the lowest-iter value that\n278\t  holds `regressions=0`. (Study: 1.0 is the only zero-regression row; α>1.0\n279\t  breaks catastrophically — confirm the cliff, don't cross it. If the sweep\n280\t  selects α<1.0, change the commit verb from \"drop\" to \"reduce\".)\n281\t- **Commit 7 — cycle `WINDOW`, `REL`** (and optionally `DELTA_CAP`). Sweep at the\n282\t  α chosen in commit 6 (the threshold's safe value depends on the contraction\n283\t  profile α sets). Adopt the tightest thresholds with `regressions=0`.\n284\t- **Commit 8 — `DEFAULT_TOL`.** This interacts with α, so do a **joint (α, tol)\n285\t  sweep**, not a one-knob sweep (the study's central methodology lesson:\n286\t  one-knob-at-a-time misled here). Adopt the loosest tol that holds\n287\t  `regressions=0` at the chosen α.\n288\t- **Commit 1's initial thresholds** are just a safe conservative baseline; they\n289\t  do not need their own sweep (commit 7 sets the final cycle thresholds).\n290\t\n291\tRecord each sweep (the iter/regression curve) as report data under\n292\t`jar/overnight-exploration/` — it is our own evidence, replacing reliance on the\n293\tstudy's figures.\n294\t\n295\t---\n296\t\n297\t## 7. Commit messages\n298\t\n299\tMatch the existing `master` subject style — bare, lowercase, imperative, **no\n300\ttype prefix, no hardcoded numbers in the subject**, one change each (cf. master's\n301\t\"add sibling-callee blocking and relaxation to fix fan-out models\", \"implement\n302\toptimised mvald\", \"improve host-layer infinite server handling\"). Put the\n303\tfine-tuned value our sweep selected in the commit **body**, not the subject.\n304\tMaster subjects carry **no Co-Authored-By trailer** — match that unless told\n305\totherwise.\n306\t\n307\t1. `add limit-cycle detection to the outer fixed-point loop`\n308\t2. `cache LqnGraph topological queries`\n309\t3. `cache per-network layer and class lookups, inline default sweep`\n310\t4. `read findCallerTask from the struct caller relation`\n311\t5. `warm-start clients delays from a closed-form lqn estimate`\n312\t6. `drop fan-out caller and INF-task under-relaxation`\n313\t7. `tighten the limit-cycle detection window`\n314\t8. `loosen convergence tolerance`\n315\t\n316\tFor commits 2–4, note in the body that the change is allocation/hotspot/\n317\tarchitecture-motivated at wall-clock parity on the corpus (not a measured corpus\n318\tspeedup), consistent with perf-section-notes §2. For commits 1, 6, 7, 8, state\n319\tthe value chosen and the sweep that selected it.\n320\t\n321\t**Ask for explicit confirmation of each commit message before committing**\n322\t(CLAUDE.md git rules). Branch off `master`; never commit without consent.\n323\t\n324\t---\n325\t\n326\t## 8. Pushback / risks to keep honest\n327\t\n328\t1. **Logic fidelity comes from porting validated hunks, not re-writing** (§4);\n329\t   the constant *values* are ours (§6). The end-state check separates the two:\n330\t   logic must match accumulate-2, values are first-party.\n331\t2. **One hard ordering constraint:** the under-relaxation value (commit 6) before\n332\t   the cycle-window tighten (commit 7) and the tolerance loosening (commit 8) —\n333\t   the latter two are only safe once the step is un-damped. This is why E14 is\n334\t   split from E2 and deferred to commit 7, and why tolerance is swept last.\n335\t3. **Commits 3 and 4 are within noise** (commit 2 carries E8, the one clean win\n336\t   vs master). Don't manufacture per-commit runtime wins for the caches; verify\n337\t   iter parity + bit-identical output + no regression.\n338\t4. **Commit 4 is a replace, not an add** (§4b) — `grep callerOfTask` must return\n339\t   nothing afterwards.\n340\t5. **Re-tuning may shift values off the study's** — that's expected and wanted.\n341\t   If it does, the final output won't be bit-identical to accumulate-2; it must\n342\t   still hold `regressions=0` against the LN reference, and our values + sweep\n343\t   become the cited evidence.\n344\t6. **The (α, tol) cliff