or\n  thresholds — are **re-derived by our own sweeps** on the verify branch (§6).\n  The study's values are the *starting hypothesis*, not the answer to copy. Our\n  first-party sweep is itself report data.\n\nPerformance is **not** strictly gated. We do not require the documented per-step\nfigures to reproduce — different (grouped) order, re-tuned values. We require:\nno clear regression, and a per-feature iteration-count + runtime-median delta\nrecorded wherever the signal is above noise.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The finalised set, grouped into 8 commits\n\nThe finalised set is the 11 `overnight-perf-accumulate-2` KEPT changes + the one\nsurviving struct slice (confirmed against `jar/perf-section-notes.md` §1–§4 and\n`jar/overnight-exploration/CONSOLIDATED.md` §5). Below they are **grouped** —\nexploration changes that are genuinely one change are merged into a single\ncommit. Subjects are deliberately **value-free**; the fine-tuned number each\ncommit adopts goes in the commit body once our sweep (§6) selects it.\n\n| commit | subject (master style) | merges | report § | tunable value(s) | files |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | add limit-cycle detection to the outer fixed-point loop | **E2** | §1 | cycle `WINDOW`/`REL`/`DELTA_CAP` (conservative baseline) | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n| 2 | cache LqnGraph topological queries | **E8 + S2-E1** | §2 | — | `LqnGraph.java` |\n| 3 | cache per-network layer and class lookups, inline default sweep | **S2-E2 + S2-E3** | §2 | — | `MvaInputs.java`, `LqnGraph.java`, `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n| 4 | read findCallerTask from the struct caller relation | struct slice (**replaces** part of #2 — see §4b) | §2 | — | `LqnGraph.java` |\n| 5 | warm-start clients delays from a closed-form lqn estimate | **S2-E8** | §3 | — | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n| 6 | drop fan-out caller and INF-task under-relaxation | **E7 + E12** | §4 | `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`, `D_RELAX_ALPHA` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n| 7 | tighten the limit-cycle detection window | **E14** | §4 | cycle `WINDOW`, `REL` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n| 8 | loosen convergence tolerance | **E10 + S2-E7** | §4 | `DEFAULT_TOL` | `SolverLNSimple.java` |\n\n(Study's hypothesis values, to test and likely confirm — **not** to copy\nblindly: `DEFAULT_TOL=1.5e-2`, `Z_RELAX_ALPHA=D_RELAX_ALPHA=1.0`, cycle\n`WINDOW=1`, `REL=1e-3`, `DELTA_CAP=10`.)\n\n**Why this order.**\n- **Commit 1 leads — cycle detection is a genuine standalone first win.** At a\n  conservative window it fixes the `A4_chainPlusFanout` maxIter pathology\n  (100 → ~13 iters) on its own, is safe at master's α=0.5/tol=5e-3 (no α\n  dependency), and matches the report's §1-first \"fix the algorithm before\n  tuning\" framing. Its thresholds are set conservatively here and **fine-tuned in\n  commit 7**.\n- **Commits 2–4 are the §2 caches** (iteration-neutral). Commit 4 **replaces**\n  part of commit 2 (the `findCallerTask` cache → struct read, §4b).\n- **Commit 5 is warm-start** (§3); it must follow the caches (2–3) it consumes\n  (perf-section-notes §3).\n- **Commits 6–8 are the §4 convergence tuning.** The one hard constraint:\n  **the under-relaxation value (commit 6) must precede the cycle-window tighten\n  (commit 7) and the tolerance loosening (commit 8)** — those two are only safe\n  once the per-iter step is un-damped (otherwise they false-fire / cross the\n  accuracy cliff at the damped α). So the cycle-window tightening (E14) is\n  deliberately deferred from commit 1 to commit 7: it is the *later tuning* of\n  the detector, and it depends on the commit-6 α. Tolerance is swept and set\n  **direct to its tuned value** (skipping the 1e-2 waypoint that only existed in\n  the study's measurement journey).\n\nEndpoint (full chain, both corpora): 56 pass / 3 known-fails\n(`B_scaleAxis_tasks5/10/20_fanout`, pre-existing on master), `regressions=0`,\nconstants set to our **fine-tuned first-party values**. If those land on the\nstudy's values the output is bit-identical to accumulate-2; if our sweep selects\ndifferent values, the output stays within the LN accuracy envelope and our values\nbecome the new reference (record the delta).\n\n---\n\n## 2. What to EXCLUDE (not necessary / does not belong)\n\n1. **Rejected accelerators** — all Anderson / Nesterov / Broyden / Aitken code\n   and their fields/knobs. The report covers them as \"rejected alternatives\"; no\n   production code.\n2. **The 9 `System.getProperty` sweep knobs** (`lnsimple.tol`, `lnsimple.zalpha`,\n   `lnsimple.dalpha`, `lnsimple.cycle*`, `lnsimple.warmStart`, `lnsimple.sweep`,\n   `lnsimple.aitken`, …). On `master`, bake the fine-tuned values as constants —\n   keep master's existing `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`/`D_RELAX_ALPHA`/`DEFAULT_TOL` names,\n   just change the values; do **not** introduce the `readDoubleProp`/`*_DEFAULT`\n   indirection. Knobs exist **only on the verify side-branch**, as the sweep\n   harness (§6).\n3. **`LayeredSolverResult.java` diagnostic-timing fields** (`lqnsElapsedTimeMs`\n   etc.) — unrelated SolverLQNS fields that leaked into the accumulate-2 diff\n   from skip-worktree local mods. Exclude.\n4. **The FastEval harness + fixtures + CSVs from `master`** — verification tool,\n   not a deliverable. Side-branch only (§3).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Branch strategy\n\nVerify (and sweep) on a side-branch; `master` receives only the production\ncommits.\n\n```\nmaster\n  └── perf-port                ← do ALL work here\n        V0 (test-only): FastEval + EvaluationSuite + util/DataCollector\n                        + ln-reference.tables.csv + LQNS baseline CSV\n        1..8: production commits (table above)\n```\n\nWhen verified, replay 1–8 onto `master`\n(`git rebase --onto master V0 perf-port`, or cherry-pick), dropping V0. `master`\nends with 8 clean production commits.\n\nPull the harness + data from the exploration branches onto V0:\n- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/overnight/FastEval.java`\n- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/overnight/CaptureLnReference.java`\n- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/util.java`\n- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/DataCollector.java`\n- `jar/src/test/java/jline/solvers/ln_simple/fixtures/EvaluationSuite.java`\n- `jar/overnight-exploration/data/ln-reference.tables.csv` (cached LN ref —\n  copy it; ~287 s to regenerate otherwise)\n- `report/data/f20axis-20260605T173243Z/baseline.tables.csv` (LQNS ref — copy\n  if not already on `master`)\n\n(`git checkout overnight-perf-accumulate-2 -- <test path>`;\n`git checkout overnight-perf-exploration -- <ln-reference csv>`.)\n\n**Setup risk to clear first:** FastEval reads SolverLNSimple's iteration count.\nIf that accessor exists only in the modified solver, FastEval won't compile\nagainst pristine `master`. Resolve in V0 (add the minimal read-only accessor, or\nadapt FastEval), then confirm V0 builds + runs against **unmodified** master and\nproduces a sane baseline before commit 1.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Fidelity method — port validated logic, then fine-tune the numbers\n\nSeparate the two concerns: the **logic** is ported faithfully; the **constants**\nare our own.\n\n1. **Establish the faithful end-state first, using the study's values.** Take\n   accumulate-2's `SolverLNSimple.java`, `LqnGraph.java`, `MvaInputs.java`;\n   remove the accelerator/knob code (§2); set the tunable constants to the\n   study's hypothesis values (`tol=1.5e-2`, `α=1.0`, `WINDOW=1`, `REL=1e-3`,\n   `DELTA_CAP=10`); apply the struct `findCallerTask` change (§4b). Build + run\n   FastEval. **With the study's values this must reproduce the validated result\n   bit-identically** (56/3, regressions=0, iters 186/192). That proves the\n   **logic** port is faithful — independent of what we later tune to. *Keep this\n   as the logic-reference target.*\n2. **Decompose into the 8 grouped commits**, starting from master, in the §1\n   order. Each slice is lifted from the validated end-state code, so the kept\n   logic is byte-faithful — you choose *when* each validated change appears, not\n   rewrite it. For the commits that carry a tunable value (1, 6, 7, 8), run the\n   sweep (§6) on the verify branch and **bake the value our sweep selects**, not\n   the study's by default.\n3. **End-state fidelity check (mandatory).** After commit 8,\n   `git diff master..perf-port -- <the three solver files>` must equal the\n   logic-reference diff from (1) **modulo the tunable constant values** — i.e.\n   the kept logic, accelerator/knob removals, struct slice, and constants all\n   present, with the constants holding *our* fine-tuned numbers. Anything else\n   (logic that differs) is unintended divergence.\n\nJava 8 compatibility applies to all `jar/` production code (no `var`,\n`Collectors.toList()` not `Stream.toList()`, etc. — CLAUDE.md).\n\n### 4a. Where each commit's diff lives (source map)\n\nRead with `git show <commit> -- <solver file>` (and, for a file's validated\nend-state, `git diff master overnight-perf-accumulate-2 -- <file>`). Read, then\nslice — do **not** cherry-pick out of order, context won't line up.\n\n| commit | merges | source commit(s) | branch | slicing notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | E2 | `e906ddaed` | accumulate-2 | cycle block + state vars; start at a conservative window/rel (study's `WINDOW=3, REL=1e-4, DELTA_CAP=10`) — fine-tuned in commit 7 |\n| 2 | E8 | `ffbe2ed81` | accumulate-2 | name cache + `WeakHashMap` + volatile fast-path |\n|   | S2-E1 | `8dee2893c` | accumulate-2 | the ~17 derived-quantity cache entries (same `ModelCache`) |\n| 3 | S2-E2 | `27e58174b` | accumulate-2 | `LayerInfo` cache in MvaInputs + `invalidateAllLayerCaches` call in SolverLNSimple |\n|   | S2-E3 | `7f888b418` | accumulate-2 | class-lookup caches + sibling-mean hoist + inline bounce sweep |\n| 4 | struct findCallerTask | `lqngraph-struct-migration` **tip** (net) | lqngraph-struct-migration | **Do not apply `5b6565d9e` as a patch** — it's a delta on a reverted predicate migration. Read the *net* region (`git show lqngraph-struct-migration:.../LqnGraph.java`) and reproduce against the commit-3 state. See §4b. |\n| 5 | S2-E8 | `f3d557efd` | exploration-2 | take only `applyLqnWarmStart` + its constructor call; this commit also adds Anderson scaffolding — exclude it; warm-start is off-by-default here, bake it ON |\n| 6 | E7 | `f753f71be` | accumulate-2 | `Z_RELAX_ALPHA` — sweep, set to tuned value (study: 1.0) |\n|   | E12 | `09d1087be` | accumulate-2 | `D_RELAX_ALPHA` — sweep, set to tuned value (study: 1.0; adjacent constant) |\n| 7 | E14 | `fea59cb05` | accumulate-2 | cycle `WINDOW`/`REL` — sweep at the commit-6 α, set to tuned value (study: `WINDOW=1, REL=1e-3`) |\n| 8 | E10 + S2-E7 | `197b93c9a`, `1919f0ba3` | accumulate-2 / exploration-2 | `DEFAULT_TOL` — joint (α, tol) sweep, set **direct** to tuned value (study: 1.5e-2; skip the 1e-2 waypoint) |\n\n**Avoid `ac3b6f27d`** (accumulate-2's bundled \"S2-E4..E8\") — it squashes the\nrejected accelerators with warm-start + tol. Use the exploration-2 commits for\ncommits 5 and 8 so the accelerator code is never in view.\n\n### 4b. Commit 2 ↔ commit 4 overlap — `findCallerTask` is the ONLY delegation\n\nCommit 4 is the one place the struct **takes burden off** the commit-2 cache. It\nis a **replace, not an add** — get this wrong and you ship both representations.\n\n| `ModelCache` field added in commit 2 | commit 4 |\n|---|---|\n| `callerOfTask` (`Map<String,String>`, lazy OO walk, the `findCallerTask` answer) | **REMOVE** — delete the field, its `put`/`get`/`containsKey` in `findCallerTask`, and the OO walk |\n| `taskByName`, `entryByName` | keep (struct returns no objects) |\n| `taskHasSyncCallees`, `callerFansOut`, `isInfScheduledTask`, `isInfProcessor`, `taskHasAndFork` | keep cached-OO — the full migration tried to delegate these and was **reverted/rejected**; only `findCallerTask` survived |\n\nCommit 4 adds: `callerOfT` (`int[]`, callee t-index → first sync-caller t-index),\n`taskIndexByName` (`Map<String,Integer>`), `taskNameByT` (`String[]`), and\n`buildCallerRelation(model, mc)` (derives all three from\n`model.getStruct().issynccaller`, called from `cacheFor`). `findCallerTask`'s\nbody becomes `name → taskIndexByName → callerOfT[t] → taskNameByT[caller]`.\n\n**Trap:** the `lqngraph-struct-migration` branch left `callerOfTask` *declared\nbut dead* after the switch. Our clean port must delete it. After commit 4:\n`grep callerOfTask` returns **nothing**; `grep callerOfT` returns the struct\narray. That grep is the no-overlap check.\n\nThe other caches (S2-E1 derived quantities in commit 2; S2-E2/E3 in commit 3)\nare **not** touched by the struct slice — no overlap there.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Per-commit gate (relaxed — regressions only, plus recorded stats)\n\nAfter each commit, build (`cd jar && mvn -Dtmp=true compile -DskipTests`) and run\nFastEval on the 59-fixture fast set. Gate:\n\n- **No accuracy regression** — 56 pass / 3 known-fails holds, `regressions=0`,\n  per-fixture max-slack vs LN within tolerance. On the iteration-neutral commits\n  (2, 3, 4) the output must be **bit-identical** to the previous commit; a slack\n  change there means the port diverged — stop and fix. (Commit 5 warm-start may\n  shift the trajectory but must stay within tolerance; commits 1, 6, 7, 8 change\n  iters by design.)\n- **No efficiency regression** — iteration count must not *increase* vs the\n  previous commit, and runtime median must not *clearly* worsen (beyond the\n  ~1.7× noise floor).\n- **Do not require the documented chronological figures** — grouped/different\n  order, re-tuned values; they won't match.\n\n**Per-feature stats (report deliverable, recorded not gated).** FastEval reports\niters + runtime each run, so record per commit: iteration-count before→after,\nruntime median + [min,max] over ≥3 warmup + ≥5 timed runs, and — for commits 1,\n6, 7, 8 — the **sweep curve** that selected the value (§6), which is first-party\ntuning evidence for the report. Honest reading:\n- Commit 1 (cycle detection): deterministic iter drop, headlined by\n  `A4_chainPlusFanout` 100 → ~13 — the genuine standalone first win, citable.\n- Commits 6, 7, 8: deterministic iter-count deltas at the chosen values — real,\n  citable numbers, with our own sweep behind them.\n- Commit 2: contains E8, the one clean wall-clock win vs master (large runtime\n  drop). It also carries S2-E1's derived cache (load-bearing per\n  perf-section-notes §2); per-layer attribution is via the ablation flags on the\n  verify branch, not via the commit split.\n- Commits 3, 4: within the 1.7× noise floor — log as \"within noise\", don't\n  invent a win.\n\nA within-noise runtime wobble on a cache commit is expected and does **not** block\nit; only a *clear* regression blocks.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Fine-tuning the values ourselves (required, on the verify branch)\n\nEvery tunable number is re-derived by our own sweep — the study's values are the\nhypothesis, not the answer. Mechanism: keep temporary `System.getProperty` knobs\n**on the verify branch only**; sweep; then bake the selected value into the\nproduction commit (which ships a bare constant, no knob).\n\nWhat to sweep, and how:\n- **Commit 6 — under-relaxation `Z_RELAX_ALPHA`, `D_RELAX_ALPHA`.** Sweep each\n  over (e.g.) {0.5, 0.7, 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.2}. Adopt the lowest-iter value that\n  holds `regressions=0`. (Study: 1.0 is the only zero-regression row; α>1.0\n  breaks catastrophically — confirm the cliff, don't cross it. If the sweep\n  selects α<1.0, change the commit verb from \"drop\" to \"reduce\".)\n- **Commit 7 — cycle `WINDOW`, `REL`** (and optionally `DELTA_CAP`). Sweep at the\n  α chosen in commit 6 (the threshold's safe value depends on the contraction\n  profile α sets). Adopt the tightest thresholds with `regressions=0`.\n- **Commit 8 — `DEFAULT_TOL`.** This interacts with α, so do a **joint (α, tol)\n  sweep**, not a one-knob sweep (the study's central methodology lesson:\n  one-knob-at-a-time misled here). Adopt the loosest tol that holds\n  `regressions=0` at the chosen α.\n- **Commit 1's initial thresholds** are just a safe conservative baseline; they\n  do not need their own sweep (commit 7 sets the final cycle thresholds).\n\nRecord each sweep (the iter/regression curve) as report data under\n`jar/overnight-exploration/` — it is our own evidence, replacing reliance on the\nstudy's figures.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Commit messages\n\nMatch the existing `master` subject style — bare, lowercase, imperative, **no\ntype prefix, no hardcoded numbers in the subject**, one change each (cf. master's\n\"add sibling-callee blocking and relaxation to fix fan-out models\", \"implement\noptimised mvald\", \"improve host-layer infinite server handling\"). Put the\nfine-tuned value our sweep selected in the commit **body**, not the subject.\nMaster subjects carry **no Co-Authored-By trailer** — match that unless told\notherwise.\n\n1. `add limit-cycle detection to the outer fixed-point loop`\n2. `cache LqnGraph topological queries`\n3. `cache per-network layer and class lookups, inline default sweep`\n4. `read findCallerTask from the struct caller relation`\n5. `warm-start clients delays from a closed-form lqn estimate`\n6. `drop fan-out caller and INF-task under-relaxation`\n7. `tighten the limit-cycle detection window`\n8. `loosen convergence tolerance`\n\nFor commits 2–4, note in the body that the change is allocation/hotspot/\narchitecture-motivated at wall-clock parity on the corpus (not a measured corpus\nspeedup), consistent with perf-section-notes §2. For commits 1, 6, 7, 8, state\nthe value chosen and the sweep that selected it.\n\n**Ask for explicit confirmation of each commit message before committing**\n(CLAUDE.md git rules). Branch off `master`; never commit without consent.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Pushback / risks to keep honest\n\n1. **Logic fidelity comes from porting validated hunks, not re-writing** (§4);\n   the constant *values* are ours (§6). The end-state check separates the two:\n   logic must match accumulate-2, values are first-party.\n2. **One hard ordering constraint:** the under-relaxation value (commit 6) before\n   the cycle-window tighten (commit 7) and the tolerance loosening (commit 8) —\n   the latter two are only safe once the step is un-damped. This is why E14 is\n   split from E2 and deferred to commit 7, and why tolerance is swept last.\n3. **Commits 3 and 4 are within noise** (commit 2 carries E8, the one clean win\n   vs master). Don't manufacture per-commit runtime wins for the caches; verify\n   iter parity + bit-identical output + no regression.\n4. **Commit 4 is a replace, not an add** (§4b) — `grep callerOfTask` must return\n   nothing afterwards.\n5. **Re-tuning may shift values off the study's** — that's expected and wanted.\n   If it does, the final output won't be bit-identical to accumulate-2; it must\n   still hold `regressions=0` against the LN reference, and our values + sweep\n   become the cited evidence.\n6. **The (α, tol) cliff is sharp; failures past it are catastrophic**\n   (slack 1e15-class). Our sweep must confirm the cliff and stop one notch inside\n   it — do not adopt a value past the last zero-regression point.\n7. **The current branch `lnstruct-migration-20260609` is the REJECTED full\n   struct migration** (bit-identical, wall-clock parity). Only its surgical\n   `findCallerTask` slice (commit 4) is kept. Do not port the rest.\n8. **Keep `master` untouched until the port begins** — the exploration uses it as\n   ground truth. Branch first.\n","numLines":352,"startLine":1,"totalLines":352}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf5b8b63-6384-4946-b120-f8ceac1b778b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev","sessionId":"367791ef-ba0c-4f75-943f-87a55717b89c","version":"2.1.168","gitBranch":"lnstruct-migration-20260609"}
