{"parentUuid":"651a9cd4-f111-4eba-96e4-4de74aac5b3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"aa89a352-c340-4c67-ba47-02402f7ad742","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CvJGsAFMdF4iTUKLzEUq2q","type":"tool_result","content":"commit ffbe2ed81a748de0c4ed319d48d3c96e92ef8c5c\nAuthor: Alex Slater <as4322@ic.ac.uk>\nDate:   Sat Jun 6 10:21:31 2026 +0100\n\n    E8: per-model memoised name lookups in LqnGraph\n    \n    Adds WeakHashMap<LayeredNetwork, ModelCache> caching findTask, findEntry, findCallerTask, isInfScheduledTask, isInfProcessor, taskHasSyncCallees, callerFansOut, taskHasAndFork. These are O(N) linear scans in the hot iter loop — profiling flagged findEntry (54 samples) and findCallerTask (26 samples, quadratic via findEntry) as the top non-EJML hotspots.\n    \n    Iters: 311 (unchanged). Runtime: ~1009 ms -> ~497 ms median across 5 runs (-51 %), well beyond the 1.7x project noise floor.\n    \n    Cache fields are populated lazily on first call per model; safe because the queried properties are topological / never change during a solve.\n    \n    (cherry picked from commit 0f8d03a73aa9b4cc11fa9fde00f6328cb1cec1e7)\n\ndiff --git a/jar/src/main/kotlin/jline/solvers/ln_simple/LqnGraph.java b/jar/src/main/kotlin/jline/solvers/ln_simple/LqnGraph.java\nindex 1c75067ef..e0f8940cb 100644\n--- a/jar/src/main/kotlin/jline/solvers/ln_simple/LqnGraph.java\n+++ b/jar/src/main/kotlin/jline/solvers/ln_simple/LqnGraph.java\n@@ -45,6 +45,50 @@ public final class LqnGraph {\n \n     private LqnGraph() {}\n \n+    // =================================================================================\n+    //  Per-model memoisation\n+    //\n+    //  Profiling (JFR, 2026-06-06) showed findEntry/findCallerTask as the top\n+    //  non-EJML CPU hotspots: both are O(N) linear name scans called from the\n+    //  per-iteration coupling loop, and findCallerTask calls findEntry inside\n+    //  its inner loops, making it quadratic.\n+    //\n+    //  Most 