"main\" class); falls back\n47\t     *  to the very first class of any kind when the layer has no active customers. */\n48\t    public static JobClass getMainClass(Network net) {\n49\t        for (JobClass jc : net.getClasses()) {\n50\t            if (jc instanceof ClosedClass && ((ClosedClass) jc).getNumberOfJobs() > 0) {\n51\t                return jc;\n52\t            }\n53\t        }\n54\t        return net.getClasses().get(0);\n55\t    }\n56\t\n57\t    /** Closed classes with N &gt; 0. Classes with N = 0 are filtered so disabled\n58\t     *  classes (e.g. the aggregate-T class in rebuilt Case-B layers) do not appear\n59\t     *  in the MVA matrices. */\n60\t    public static List<ClosedClass> getClosedClasses(Network net) {\n61\t        List<ClosedClass> result = new ArrayList<ClosedClass>();\n62\t        for (JobClass jc : net.getClasses()) {\n63\t            if (jc instanceof ClosedClass && ((ClosedClass) jc).getNumberOfJobs() > 0) {\n64\t                result.add((ClosedClass) jc);\n65\t            }\n66\t        }\n67\t        return result;\n68\t    }\n69\t\n70\t    /**\n71\t     * Build the {@code (numNodes × numClasses)} demand matrix L. Delay nodes get\n72\t     * demand 0 (their service time enters through Z, not L). For non-Delay\n73\t     * stations:\n74\t     * <ul>\n75\t     *   <li>Take the class's own service-process mean if it is not NaN.</li>"}]},"uuid":"d0400091-47c1-4eb6-bbac-6df9fb6fdb27","timestamp":"2026-06-09T22:59:25.398Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev/jar/src/main/kotlin/jline/solvers/ln_simple/mva/MvaInputs.java","content":"package jline.solvers.ln_simple.mva;\n\nimport jline.io.Ret;\nimport jline.lang.ClosedClass;\nimport jline.lang.JobClass;\nimport jline.lang.Network;\nimport jline.lang.nodes.Delay;\nimport jline.lang.nodes.Node;\nimport jline.lang.nodes.Queue;\nimport jline.lang.nodes.ServiceStation;\nimport jline.lang.nodes.Station;\nimport jline.solvers.ln_simple.SolverLNSimple;\nimport jline.util.matrix.Matrix;\n\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n/**\n * MVA matrix-builder utilities for {@link SolverLNSimple}.\n *\n * <p>Each ensemble layer is a two-node closed network (one {@code Clients} delay\n * plus one queue). These helpers assemble the inputs to the backing\n * {@code pfqn_mvams} routine:\n * <ul>\n *   <li>{@code L} — service-demand matrix at non-Delay stations</li>\n *   <li>{@code N} — per-class population vector</li>\n *   <li>{@code Z} — per-class think time from the {@code Clients} delay</li>\n *   <li>{@code S} — per-station server counts ({@code Integer.MAX_VALUE} mapped to {@code N_total})</li>\n * </ul>\n */\npublic final class MvaInputs {\n\n    private MvaInputs() {}\n\n    /** All Queue and Delay nodes in {@code layer}, preserving network order. */\n    public static List<Node> getQueueNodes(Network layer) {\n        List<Node> nodes = new ArrayList<Node>();\n        for (Node node : layer.getNodes()) {\n            if (node instanceof Queue || node instanceof Delay) {\n                nodes.add(node);\n            }\n        }\n        return nodes;\n    }\n\n    /** First closed class with positive population (the \"main\" class); falls back\n     *  to the very first class of any kind when the layer has no active customers. */\n    public static JobClass getMainClass(Network net) {\n        for (JobClass jc : net.getClasses()) {\n            if (jc instanceof ClosedClass && ((ClosedClass) jc).getNumberOfJobs() > 0) {\n                return jc;\n            }\n        }\n        return net.getClasses().get(0);\n    }\n\n    /** Closed classes with N &gt; 0. Classes with N = 0 are filtered so disabled\n     *  classes (e.g. the aggregate-T class in rebuilt Case-B layers) do not appear\n     *  in the MVA matrices. */\n    public static List<ClosedClass> getClosedClasses(Network net) {\n        List<ClosedClass> result = new ArrayList<ClosedClass>();\n        for (JobClass jc : net.getClasses()) {\n            if (jc instanceof ClosedClass && ((ClosedClass) jc).getNumberOfJobs() > 0) {\n                result.add((ClosedClass) jc);\n            }\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Build the {@code (numNodes × numClasses)} demand matrix L. Delay nodes get\n     * demand 0 (their service time enters through Z, not L). For non-Delay\n     * stations:\n     * <ul>\n     *   <li>Take the class's own service-process mean if it is not NaN.</li>","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":318}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5529bc8d-6f15-41ec-9dd3-5b8854f8a60b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev","sessionId":"367791ef-ba0c-4f75-943f-87a55717b89c","version":"2.1.168","gitBranch":"perf-port"}
