{"parentUuid":"c76fad8b-d7f8-45e1-b931-336e21443a34","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Ff49nbAs63BH2Kwv1fovht","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two good questions — let me address both directly.\n\n**1. Did I performance-test commit 2?**\n\nPartially, and I should be honest about the limits. I ran FastEval with `warmup=3, repeats=5` on commit 2 and the total median time came out ~1055 ms vs the master baseline's ~1739 ms — consistent with E8 being the one real wall-clock win (the reference reported ~1009→497 ms, ~2×). **But** those totals are from *separate JVM invocations on a shared machine* whose load visibly varied (identical work took 195–246 s elapsed across runs), so it's indicative, not a clean isolated A/B. The per-fixture `time_med` (5 repeats) within each run is stable, but cross-commit totals carry machine noise. I did **not** yet do a rigorous back-to-back measurement — correctness was gated bit-identically, which is the hard requirement, but the citable runtime delta (plan §5 deliverable) deserves a proper A/B.\n\n**2. What sweep for commit 3?**\n\nNone — and this is a naming collision in the plan that's worth clearing up. \"inline default **sweep**\" in commit 3 refers to the **layer-traversal sweep**: the outer loop visits layers in a bounce order `0,1,…,N-1,N-2,…,1`. S2-E3 inlines that index arithmetic directly into the loop (dropping the `computeSweepLayerIndex` dispatch). It is **not** a parameter sweep. Commit 3 is an iteration-neutral cache — gated bit-identical, **no tunable values**.\n\nThe only **parameter sweeps** in the whole plan are commits **6** (`Z/D_RELAX_ALPHA`), **7** (cycle `WINDOW`/`REL`), and **8** (`DEFAULT_TOL`) — those carry the tunable constants §6 says to re-derive ourselves.\n\n**Proposal:** let me finish commit 3 (nearly done — MvaInputs is done, SolverLNSimple changes remain), then run one clean back-to-back A/B across commits 1→2→3 (each rebuilt and FastEval'd in sequence, a couple of passes) to get the real runtime deltas — that gives the citable E8 win for commit 2 and confirms commit 3 is within noise, which is exactly the §5 report data. Sound good? Meanwhile I'll continue building commit 3."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":175,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":301799,"output_tokens":4629,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":175,"output_tokens":4629,"cache_read_input_tokens":301799,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbtWzDSWZea5NgKD1rKMy","type":"assistant","uuid":"518dd890-0bc9-4365-82e0-fc6fd59b9a9c","timestamp":"2026-06-09T23:02:08.725Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/alex/Documents/FYP/line-dev","sessionId":"367791ef-ba0c-4f75-943f-87a55717b89c","version":"2.1.168","gitBranch":"perf-port"}
